WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:16.471
"Hey! What are you doing?" Zann cried.

2
00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:19.637
Zing glanced at his master and then at Boz.

3
00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:23.077
With a burst of smoke, the dragon leaped into the air.

4
00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:30.038
"Oh!" Boz exclaimed as the little dragon flew at him, snatched the stone out of his hand, and swallowed it.

5
00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:34.819
"Give that back or you'll be sorry, you scaly scoundrel!"

6
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:40.369
Teplo put a hand on Boz's arm. He had already undone Boz's Lip-Zip spell.

7
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.216
"Settle down, old friend," Teplo said soothingly.

8
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:48.965
"It won't do any harm to let the boy keep his souvenir, eh?"

9
00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:55.604
Boz glared at Zing and sighed. "I suppose you're right," he said, straightening his clothes.

10
00:00:55.605 --> 00:01:02.109
"Come, Teplo. I promised the king I'd fetch those texts from the archives right away."

11
00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.971
Teplo nodded and then glanced at the kids.

12
00:01:04.972 --> 00:01:07.281
"See you at Saffa's in an hour."

13
00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:10.813
"We'll be there," Gliss promised.

14
00:01:10.814 --> 00:01:15.515
"What was that all about?" Perda wondered after the two old men zapped away.

15
00:01:15.516 --> 00:01:19.101
"I have no idea." Zann whistled for Zing.

16
00:01:19.102 --> 00:01:22.637
The little dragon flew over and landed in front of him.

17
00:01:22.638 --> 00:01:26.583
Zing shot out a burst of flame. The stone tumbled out with it.

18
00:01:26.584 --> 00:01:33.995
Zann grabbed the stone. "Ow!" he blurted out, juggling it from one hand to the other to keep it from burning his skin.

19
00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:39.842
"Extinguish!" he said, rubbing one leg against the other to create enough friction for the spell.

20
00:01:39.843 --> 00:01:43.078
Instantly the stone felt cool in Zann's hand.

21
00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:45.423
Gliss leaned over to peer at it.

22
00:01:45.424 --> 00:01:49.146
"Hey, it doesn't look burned at all," she said.

23
00:01:49.147 --> 00:01:53.830
"It must be fireproof," Darb said. "I wonder where it came from."

24
00:01:53.831 --> 00:02:01.007
"Me too." Zann turned the stone over in his hand. "Teplo seemed to recognize it."

25
00:02:01.008 --> 00:02:10.860
"So did Boz," Gliss said. "I can't believe he did a Lip-Zip spell on Teplo! He's lucky Teplo didn't get mad."

26
00:02:10.861 --> 00:02:18.052
"Yeah," Perda said. "If they won't tell us about the stone, maybe we can try to research it on our own."

27
00:02:18.053 --> 00:02:22.932
Zann sighed. "We can try. But we're running out of time.

28
00:02:22.933 --> 00:02:30.236
Once we're back in Swamp Bottom, it will be much harder to do anything." He leaned over and scratched Zing.

29
00:02:30.237 --> 00:02:35.342
"Anyway, thanks for getting the stone back for me, little buddy."

30
00:02:35.343 --> 00:02:36.989
Honk! Honk!

31
00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:41.406
Zann jumped back as Teplo's sniffer goose leaped out the front door at him.

32
00:02:41.407 --> 00:02:44.851
"Quit it!" said Zann, dodging the goose's beak.

33
00:02:44.852 --> 00:02:50.729
"Down, girl," Teplo added with a chuckle. "It's just us."

34
00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:55.643
The goose backed down, but her beady little eyes were still trained on Zann.

35
00:02:55.644 --> 00:03:00.192
Zann ignored her as he followed Teplo, Boz, and Darb into the house.

36
00:03:00.193 --> 00:03:06.976
The four of them had just returned from that evening's dinner party, though Zann had been too distracted to enjoy himself much.

37
00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:10.755
"Anyone care for a game of exploding dominoes?"

38
00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:15.715
Teplo rubbed his hands together to trade his party clothes for his usual robe and sandals.

39
00:03:15.716 --> 00:03:21.310
"No thanks," Zann said. "I'm pretty tired. I think I'll go to bed."

40
00:03:21.311 --> 00:03:23.875
"Me too," Darb said.

41
00:03:23.876 --> 00:03:27.574
Zann and Darb headed upstairs to the guest room they were sharing.

42
00:03:27.575 --> 00:03:31.285
When the door shut behind them, Zann spun to face his friend.

43
00:03:31.286 --> 00:03:34.849
"I can't stand this anymore," he blurted out.

44
00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.763
"I need to know what happened to my parents!"

45
00:03:37.764 --> 00:03:41.186
"I understand," Darb said. "Maybe Boz—"

46
00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:48.540
"Forget Boz!" Zann interrupted. "I need to come up with a plan to find my parents on my own."

47
00:03:48.541 --> 00:03:54.939
He paced back and forth. "Maybe I should just try jumping into a wormhole like I said before."

48
00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.764
Bang! A small explosion came from downstairs.

49
00:03:58.765 --> 00:04:01.819
Boz and Teplo were apparently playing dominoes.

50
00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.834
"What?" Darb sounded alarmed. "Zann, that's crazy!

51
00:04:05.835 --> 00:04:10.350
It's no plan at all. You'll end up lost just like your parents!"

52
00:04:10.351 --> 00:04:13.287
"Well, it would be better than doing nothing!"

53
00:04:13.288 --> 00:04:16.346
Zann stopped pacing and glared at his friend.

54
00:04:16.347 --> 00:04:22.409
"Morb and Wyssa both seem to think my parents are still out there somewhere in the vortex!"

55
00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.494
Another domino exploded.

56
00:04:24.495 --> 00:04:30.257
"I know," Darb said. "But you need help from someone who knows more about these things.

57
00:04:30.258 --> 00:04:33.409
Why don't you try talking to your grandfather again?"

58
00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.433
Zann rolled his eyes. "Are you kidding?

59
00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:41.111
You saw how Boz reacted when he saw the stone."

60
00:04:41.112 --> 00:04:44.769
Darb shrugged. "I think you just took him by surprise.

61
00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.235
Boz is a reasonable person, and he cares about you.

62
00:04:48.236 --> 00:04:51.959
Maybe if you ask nicely, he'll talk to you about what's going on."

63
00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.642
"Do you really think so?" Zann was dubious.

64
00:04:55.643 --> 00:04:59.796
Boz hadn't seemed very reasonable when he'd snatched the stone earlier.

65
00:04:59.797 --> 00:05:03.833
"It's worth a try," said Darb. "What have you got to lose?"

66
00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:08.831
Zann hesitated. But finally he nodded. He trusted Darb's judgment.

67
00:05:08.832 --> 00:05:12.187
"Okay," he said. "I'll talk to him."

68
00:05:12.188 --> 00:05:14.845
Zann opened the door and headed for the stairs.

69
00:05:14.846 --> 00:05:18.370
At the top he took a deep breath to calm himself.

70
00:05:18.371 --> 00:05:23.608
The dominoes had stopped exploding, and he could hear Boz and Teplo talking quietly.

71
00:05:23.609 --> 00:05:27.301
Feeling curious, Zann leaned forward to listen.

72
00:05:27.302 --> 00:05:31.610
". . . and that doesn't leave much time," Teplo was saying.

73
00:05:31.611 --> 00:05:39.223
"Perhaps not," Boz replied. "But the plan is set. We leave First City tomorrow afternoon."

74
00:05:39.224 --> 00:05:44.163
Zann gasped and backed away from the staircase. Tomorrow afternoon?

75
00:05:44.164 --> 00:05:49.506
It was too late to try to talk to Boz about the stone. Zann had to act now!

76
00:05:49.507 --> 00:05:51.468
He hurried back to the guest room.

77
00:05:51.469 --> 00:05:54.529
Darb looked surprised. "What happened?"

78
00:05:54.530 --> 00:06:00.133
"Nothing. I, uh, decided I'm too tired to argue with Boz right now."

79
00:06:00.134 --> 00:06:06.073
Zann zapped himself into his pajamas and climbed into bed. "I'll talk to him tomorrow."

80
00:06:06.074 --> 00:06:10.069
"Oh. Okay, good-night." Darb got into bed too.

81
00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.976
Zann rubbed his fingers to extinguish the light.

82
00:06:12.977 --> 00:06:16.902
Then he lay in the dark, staring at the moonlit ceiling.

83
00:06:16.903 --> 00:06:19.761
He felt guilty about lying to his best friend.

84
00:06:19.762 --> 00:06:30.034
But Zann's plans had changed, and Darb definitely wouldn't approve of what Zann was going to do next.
